    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `membershipTier` is a derived, read-only field computed from data already stored on the `Owner` entity (`namesakeCount` and `email`), so I added it at the response-mapping layer \u2014 which covers both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}` responses.\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` string property (read-only) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression alongside the existing derived fields:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"membershipTier\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0\n           && owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty() ? \\\"SILVER\\\" : \\\"BRONZE\\\")\")\n   ```\n   Returns `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`. The null guards keep it safe against a missing count or absent email (both yield `BRONZE`).\n\nTest results: `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` (unique owner + email \u2192 SILVER) and `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` (no email \u2192 BRONZE) both pass.",
